ly as the sample gets more dilute, which is what saturation would produce. The reader therefore responds proportionally in this range, and the flat line is a true stationary phase at an OD600 of about 0.44. The late biomass is at the level the undiluted readings indicate. The main uncertainty is the scatter in the multiplied-back values, about ±10%. The 15 h check is slightly high, but this is too small to suggest the reader is capping the readings."},"episode":{"assay":{"eps_lin":0.05,"n":8.0,"resolution":0.0001,"s_odeq":0.5221121549718328,"sigma_abs":0.003,"sigma_rel":0.02,"y_loq":0.03},"condition":"BIOLOGICAL_PLATEAU","episode_id":"s500006-BP","growth":{"k_odeq":0.4522232770181044,"nu":8.0,"r_per_h":0.7306024839763147,"x0_odeq":0.0131881562232988},"k_ratio":0.8661420208508671,"scenario_sha256":"5291e69c061fa42973cf541bd84b78a90770dc971227f32f052acfc404c0ce08","scenario_version":"scenario-v1","seed":500006},"events":[{"arguments":{"dilution_factor":10,"replicates":2,"time_h":18},"error":null,"index":0,"ok":true,"result":{"budget_remaining":4,"dilution_factor":10.0,"mean_reading":0.039,"readings":[0.043,0.035],"time_h":18},"tool":"measure_od","turn":1},{"arguments":{"dilution_factor":4,"replicates":2,"time_h":18},"error":null,"index":1,"ok":true,"result":{"budget_remaining":2,"dilution_factor":4.0,"mean_reading":0.1146,"readings":[0.1113,0.1179],"time_h":18},"tool":"measure_od","turn":2},{"arguments":{"dilution_factor":5,"replicates":2,"time_h":15},"error":null,"index":2,"ok":true,"result":{"budget_remaining":0,"dilution_factor":5.0,"mean_reading":0.0965,"readings":[0.0958,0.0971],"time_h":15},"tool":"measure_od","turn":3},{"arguments":{"diagnosis":"BIOMASS_AS_READ","late_biomass_estimate_od":0.44,"p_biomass_above_reading":0.15,"rationale":"The undiluted readings level off abruptly at about 0.43 from 5 h onward. That pattern could mean the reader stops responding proportionally at high density, so I tested late aliquots at several dilutions. At 18 h, the 10× diluti